    {
      "name": "planned_end_date",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_date",
      "description": "The date that something is or was planned to end, with precision of one day.",
      "comments": [
        "Used for anything with a planned end date, such as when a lease will expire, when an offer is no longer available, etc. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "planned end date"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndDate"
      ],
      "is_a": "planned_end_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndDate",
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "planned_end_date_time",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_date_time",
      "description": "The date that something is or was planned to end, with no implied precision.",
      "comments": [
        "This is an abstraction over the various precisions of planned end time, and is not expected to be asserted directly. Values of predicates with different precisions can be compared since they are all formally xsd:datetimes.",
        "This property, unlike gist:actualEndDateTime, does not have a subproperty for microsecond precision, because planned times typically are not expressed at that level of granularity. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "planned end date time"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndDateTime"
      ],
      "is_a": "end_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndDateTime",
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "planned_end_minute",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_minute",
      "description": "The date and time that something is or was planned to end, with precision of one minute.",
      "comments": [
        "Used for things like meetings and time card entries, where the hour and minute are important. Recommended usage is to zero out the seconds and microseconds to avoid spurious precision.Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T08:32:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "planned end minute"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndMinute"
      ],
      "is_a": "planned_end_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndMinute",
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "planned_end_year",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_end_year",
      "description": "The date that something is or was planned to end, with precision of one year.",
      "comments": [
        "Used for anything with a planned end date where precision of one year is sufficient. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision. Note that it is not valid to zero out months and days, so arbitrary values must be included."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-01-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "The automobile manufacturer announced that it will stop producing gas-powered vehicles in 2035.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "planned end year"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndYear"
      ],
      "is_a": "planned_end_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedEndYear",
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "planned_start_date",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_date",
      "description": "The date that something is or was planned to start, with precision of one day.",
      "comments": [
        "Used for anything with a planned start date, such as when a lease will start, when a configuration becomes available, etc. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "planned start date"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartDate"
      ],
      "is_a": "planned_start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartDate",
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "planned_start_date_time",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_date_time",
      "description": "The date and time that something is or was planned to start, with no implied precision.",
      "comments": [
        "This is an abstraction over the various precisions of planned start time, and is not expected to be asserted directly. Values of predicates with different precisions can be compared since they are all formally xsd:datetimes.",
        "This property, unlike gist:actualStartDateTime, does not have a subproperty for microsecond precision, because planned times typically are not expressed at that level of granularity. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "planned start date time"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartDateTime"
      ],
      "is_a": "start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartDateTime",
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "planned_start_minute",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_minute",
      "description": "The date and time that something is or was planned to start, with precision of one minute.",
      "comments": [
        "Used for things like meetings and time card entries, where the hour and minute are important. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the seconds and microseconds to avoid spurious precision."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T08:32:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "planned start minute"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartMinute"
      ],
      "is_a": "planned_start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartMinute",
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "planned_start_year",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/planned_start_year",
      "description": "The date that something is or was planned to start, with precision of one year.",
      "comments": [
        "Used for anything with a planned start date where precision of one year is sufficient. Typically a planned date is in the future when first captured, but when tasks run late, we leave the plan where it was and compare it to the actual. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision. Note that it is not valid to zero out months and days, so arbitrary values must be included."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-01-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "The automobile manufacturer announced that its full line-up will include only electric cars starting in 2035.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "planned start year"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartYear"
      ],
      "is_a": "planned_start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/plannedStartYear",
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "sequence",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/sequence",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "domain_includes",
          "value": "gist:OrderedMember",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "A number that specifies the position of an element within a series.",
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "sequence"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/sequence"
      ],
      "domain": "OrderedMember",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/sequence",
      "owner": "sequence",
      "range": "integer",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "start_date_time",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/start_date_time",
      "description": "The date and time that something starts.",
      "comments": [
        "This property is neutral along two dimensions: precision (e.g., day, second, millisecond) and actual vs. planned. As such, it will generally not be asserted directly except in special cases (e.g., for time intervals).",
        "Values of predicates with different precisions can be compared since they are all formally xsd:datetimes."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "start date time"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/startDateTime"
      ],
      "is_a": "at_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/startDateTime",
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "symbol",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/symbol",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "domain_includes",
          "value": "gist:UnitOfMeasure",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "A symbol for something using only ASCII characters.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The ASCII symbol for square meter is m^2.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "symbol"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/symbol"
      ],
      "domain": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/symbol",
      "owner": "symbol",
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "unique_text",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/unique_text",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "domain_includes",
          "value": "gist:ID, gist:MediaType, gist:Tag, gist:Text",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The unique string value of some content object, to be used when there is no possibility of having more than one value.",
      "comments": [
        "Note that the uniqueness only goes in one direction: a product catalog number might also be an employee ID."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The unique string for a vehicle identification number.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "unique text"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/uniqueText"
      ],
      "is_a": "contained_text",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/uniqueText",
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "domain_includes",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/domain_includes",
      "description": "Relates a property to a class that the property is expected to be used on.",
      "comments": [
        "There may be multiple domainIncludes assertions on a single property.",
        "This property is used to guide the ontology user; like all annotation properties, it does not play a role in inference."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The domain of the property gist:containedText includes gist:Tag and gist:Text.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "domain includes"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/domainIncludes"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/domainIncludes",
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_superseded_by",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/is_superseded_by",
      "description": "Relates a deprecated term to a term that replaces it, which is either an exact (in the case of simple renaming) or approximate (in the case of renaming and some semantic change) semantic match.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "gist:connectedTo was superseded by gist:isConnectedTo (renaming with no semantic change).",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "is superseded by"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/isSupersededBy"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/isSupersededBy",
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "license",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/license",
      "description": "Relates something to its conditions of use.",
      "comments": [
        "Could refer to a license object by URI or name or could consist of the license text itself."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The gist ontology is licensed under the CC By 4.0 license.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "license"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/license"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/license",
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "range_includes",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/range_includes",
      "description": "Relates a property to a class that is an expected type of its values.",
      "comments": [
        "There may be multiple rangeIncludes assertions on a single property.",
        "This property is used to guide the ontology user; like all annotation properties, it does not play a role in inference."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The range of the property gist:isCategorizedBy includes gist:Category.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "range includes"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/rangeIncludes"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/rangeIncludes",
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    }
  ],
  "classes": [
    {
      "name": "Account",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Account",
      "description": "An agreement having a balance.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Agreement & \u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_financial_balance)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A bank account, a credit card account, an accounts receivable account.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Account"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Account"
      ],
      "close_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Account"
      ],
      "is_a": "Agreement",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Account",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Address",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Address",
      "description": "A reference to a place (real or virtual) that can be located by some routing algorithm and where messages or things can be sent or received.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A PO Box, a URL to a PDF file.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Address"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Address"
      ],
      "narrow_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Address"
      ],
      "is_a": "Content",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Address",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "AddressUsageType",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/AddressUsageType",
      "description": "A category indicating the context or manner in which an address may be used.",
      "comments": [
        "If you are using temporal relations involving addresses, this category should be used to qualify the temporal relation rather than the address itself, since the same address may have different uses in different contexts, by different people and organizations, or at different times."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Billing, business, personal, postal, residence.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Address Usage Type"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:AddressUsageType"
      ],
      "is_a": "Category",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/AddressUsageType",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Agreement",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Agreement",
      "description": "A mutually understood arrangement in which two or more parties make commitments to one another.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Intention & \u2203hasParty.(gist:Organization | gist:Person) & \u22652^isDirectPartOf.gist:Commitment)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "While an agreement has two or more parties, and contains commitments which bind those parties, it will not always be necessary to instantiate each individual commitment."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A gym membership is an agreement in which the member commits to paying the gym a certain price and the gym commits to allowing access to their facilities.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Agreement"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Agreement"
      ],
      "close_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Agreement"
      ],
      "narrow_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:MasterAgreement",
        "dpv:DataProcessingAgreement"
      ],
      "is_a": "Intention",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Agreement",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Aspect",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Aspect",
      "description": "A measurable characteristic.",
      "comments": [
        "Depending on implementation, every aspect should be related to a unit group either directly or through a broader aspect. For example, angle of incidence could be related to the broader concept of angle, which in turn is related to a unit group, or it could be related directly to the unit group without the hierarchical relationship.",
        "Rule of thumb: use the least specific aspect that serves the intended purpose, increasing specificity only when required (e.g., to distinguish between two magnitudes attached to the same object)."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Length, weight, cost, cycle time, defect rate, wheelbase, billing rate.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Aspect"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Aspect"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Aspect",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "Event"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Assignment",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Assignment",
      "description": "A temporal relationship between an assignee, the thing assigned, and the resource that made the assignment.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:TemporalRelation & \u2203hasGiver.owl:Thing & \u2203isAssignmentOf.owl:Thing & \u2203isAssignmentTo.owl:Thing)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Based on the Open World Assumption, the assigner may not be asserted or known.",
        "For some assignments, such as the assignment of a person to a task, it may seem equally correct in ordinary speech to say it is an assignment of a task to a person. Since gist:isAssignmentTo and gist:isAssignmentOf have no formal domains or ranges, the choice of which predicate to use for which is left as an implementation decision. Consistency is a key consideration."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "An employee is assigned to a task by a supervisor. A person is assigned to a position.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Assignment"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Assignment"
      ],
      "close_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:NaturalPersonRole"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:RelatedParty",
        "common_domain_model:Counterparty"
      ],
      "is_a": "TemporalRelation",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Assignment",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Behavior",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Behavior",
      "description": "A category indicating the nature of an activity.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Drilling and cutting are two different kinds of manufacturing event.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Behavior"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Behavior"
      ],
      "is_a": "Category",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Behavior",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Building",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Building",
      "description": "A relatively permanent man-made structure situated on a plot of land, having a roof and walls, commonly used for dwelling, entertaining, or working.",
      "deprecated": "true",
      "comments": [
        "User discretion can be applied to edge cases: e.g., is a traditional yurt 'relatively permanently situated' although it is portable and has a tent-like construction?"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A house, school, store, factory, chicken coop.",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "Negative examples: houseboats (not built on land), caves (not man-made), food trucks and RVs (not permanently situated).",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Building"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Building"
      ],
      "is_a": "Landmark",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Building",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "BundledCatalogItem",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/BundledCatalogItem",
      "description": "Any combination of descriptions of things offered together.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:CatalogItem & \u2203^isDirectPartOf.gist:CatalogItem)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A kit containing several parts offered together; a product plus a warranty.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Bundled Catalog Item"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:BundledCatalogItem"
      ],
      "is_a": "CatalogItem",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/BundledCatalogItem",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "CatalogItem",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/CatalogItem",
      "description": "A description of a product or service to be delivered, given in a sufficient level of detail that a receiver could determine whether delivery constituted discharge of the obligation to deliver.",
      "comments": [
        "In short, an unambiguous characterization of what it is that a potential buyer is paying for."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Catalog Item"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:CatalogItem"
      ],
      "is_a": "Specification",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/CatalogItem",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Category",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Category",
      "description": "A concept or label used to categorize other instances without specifying any formal semantics.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: \u2203isAllocatedBy.(gist:IntellectualProperty | gist:Organization | gist:Person)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Often a type can be modeled either as an owl:Class or as a gist:Category. Use the latter if you don't care much about the formal structure of the different types, or if there is a whole hierarchy of types that are going to be managed by a group separate from the ontology developers. The formal structure may be defined elsewhere and linked to, if necessary."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Tags used in folksonomies; formal definitions from other systems.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Category"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Category"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Category",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "Event"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Collection",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Collection",
      "description": "A grouping of things.",
      "comments": [
        "Individuals are placed in the collection using the gist:isMemberOf property. Collections typically are created because the members are functionally connected in some way. This definition allows a collection to have zero members."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A jury is a group of people; a financial ledger is a collection of transaction entries; a route is an (ordered) collection of segments.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Collection"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Collection"
      ],
      "is_a": "Composite",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Collection",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Commitment",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Commitment",
      "description": "A promise made by a single party to one or more parties to do or not do something or act in a particular way.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Intention & (gist:Requirement | gist:Restriction) & \u2203hasGiver.(gist:Organization | gist:Person) & \u2203isCategorizedBy.gist:DegreeOfCommitment)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "A commitment is unilateral in that it is binding on only one party. This contrasts with gist:Agreement, which consists of commitments that bind two or more parties.",
        "A single commitment may be made to multiple parties at once; it is a single commitment rather than multiple commitments if the same action would fulfill the obligation to all the parties simultaneously. For example, a performer makes a single commitment to hold a performance to all ticket purchasers; by holding the performance, the commitment to all parties is fulfilled in a single action.",
        "The manner in which a commitment is binding may vary. In a business context, we are typically interested in commitments that are legally binding."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Upon selling a treasury bill, the U.S. government makes a commitment to pay the purchaser a stated amount of money at a stated time.",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "When signing an NDA, the signatory commits to keeping specified information confidential.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Commitment"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Commitment"
      ],
      "is_a": "Intention",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Commitment",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Component",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Component",
      "description": "Something that, while having an independent existence, is inherently part of or designed to be part of a larger entity, such as a system or network.",
      "comments": [
        "A component may be designed or intended as part of a whole without actually being so; e.g., a car steering wheel that is not installed in any car.",
        "Many things are in a trivial sense a part of a larger thing, but are not considered components because they are not inherently part of that larger thing. For example, while a book may be part of a library (a collection of books), it is not inherently so, and thus is not a component. A playing card, on the other hand, could be considered a component in (member of) a deck of cards. This may be use case-dependent; e.g., car parts might be modeled as components in an automobile manufacturing context but not in a retail auto parts store.",
        "Physical substances, such as ingredients in a cake batter, do not meet the independent existence criterion, so are not components.",
        "This class is not disjoint with gist:Composite, because a component may itself break down into smaller components.",
        "This is an abstract class that is not directly instantiated. Users will define subclasses that are meaningful to their domain of interest."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Component"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Component"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Component",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "PhysicalSubstance"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Composite",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Composite",
      "description": "Something which is made up of various parts or elements that are independently identifiable.",
      "comments": [
        "Some composites, like systems, networks, and ordered collections, have internal organization, while others, such as unordered collections, typically do not.",
        "This class is not disjoint with gist:Component, because a composite can itself be a component of a larger composite.",
        "This is an abstract class that will not be directly instantiated."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A library (collection of books); a network of pipes and valves; a computer network of routers and computers.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Composite"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Composite"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Composite",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "ContemporaryEvent",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/ContemporaryEvent",
      "description": "An event that has started but has not yet ended.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Event & =1actualStartDateTime & \u22640actualEndDateTime)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "When the event actually ends, it will cease being contemporary."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Contemporary Event"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:ContemporaryEvent"
      ],
      "is_a": "Event",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/ContemporaryEvent",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Content",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Content",
      "description": "Information available in some medium.",
      "comments": [
        "Categories are not content until they are written down.",
        "This class includes both abstract content and its expression, but it must have at least one expression in order to be content. For example, the idea a writer has for a book is not content until it is expressed in some form, but a single content object may have multiple expressions - e.g., the particular print and audio editions."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The literary work 'The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn' by Mark Twain, independent of any particular edition.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Content"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Content"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Content",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "GeoPoint",
        "GeoRegion",
        "Organization",
        "PhysicalIdentifiableItem",
        "PhysicalSubstance",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "ContentExpression",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/ContentExpression",
      "description": "Content reduced to text, audio, etc.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: \u2203isCategorizedBy.gist:GeneralMediaType"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "If it contains text (written or spoken), it will be expressed in a language.",
        "While the content expression is less abstract than a 'Work,' it is more abstract than the specific physical items that render the expression. For example, any physical or electronic book with ISBN-13 978-1953649805 is associated with the same content expression."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A specific print or audio edition of 'The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn,' such as the one identified by ISBN-13 978-1953649805.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Content Expression"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:ContentExpression"
      ],
      "is_a": "Content",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/ContentExpression",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "ContingentEvent",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/ContingentEvent",
      "description": "An event with a probability of happening in the future, and usually dependent upon some other event or condition.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Event & \u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_probability & \u2203isTriggeredBy.gist:Event)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A fire insurance payout is contingent on a particular building burning down; selling 20 shares of stock in a given company is contingent on the price dropping below $200/share; the death benefit payout on a life insurance policy is contingent on the death of the insured person.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Contingent Event"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:ContingentEvent"
      ],
      "is_a": "Event",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/ContingentEvent",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "ContingentObligation",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/ContingentObligation",
      "description": "An obligation that is not yet firm. There is some contingent event whose occurrence will cause the obligation to become firm.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Commitment & \u2203hasGiver.(gist:Organization | gist:Person) & \u2203isTriggeredBy.gist:Event)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "A contingent obligation might have a getter counterparty (as in the case of insurance); but it might not (as in the case of an offer)."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Contingent Obligation"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:ContingentObligation"
      ],
      "broad_mappings": [
        "dpv:Obligation"
      ],
      "is_a": "Commitment",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/ContingentObligation",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Contract",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Contract",
      "description": "An agreement which can be enforced by law.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Agreement & \u2203isUnderJurisdictionOf.gist:GovernmentOrganization)"
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Contract"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Contract"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "dpv:Contract"
      ],
      "is_a": "Agreement",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Contract",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "ContractTerm",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/ContractTerm",
      "description": "A specification of some aspect of a contract.",
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Contract Term"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:ContractTerm"
      ],
      "narrow_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:CollateralProvisions"
      ],
      "is_a": "Specification",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/ContractTerm",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "ControlledVocabulary",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/ControlledVocabulary",
      "description": "A collection of terms approved and managed by some organization or person.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Collection & \u2203isGovernedBy.(gist:Organization | gist:Person) & \u2203^isMemberOf.gist:Category)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "A controlled vocabulary is similar to a skos:ConceptScheme, but it could also be used for things that are not concepts, such as organizations, US presidents, geographic regions, etc. Hierarchical relationships between instances of the controlled vocabulary are possible."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Controlled Vocabulary"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:ControlledVocabulary"
      ],
      "is_a": "Collection",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/ControlledVocabulary",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "CountryGeoRegion",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/CountryGeoRegion",
      "description": "A geographic region governed by exactly one country government.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: =1isGovernedBy",
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:GovernedGeoRegion & \u2203isGovernedBy.gist:CountryGovernment)"
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Country Geographic Region"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:CountryGeoRegion"
      ],
      "is_a": "GovernedGeoRegion",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/CountryGeoRegion",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "CountryGovernment",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/CountryGovernment",
      "description": "A government organization which asserts both sovereignty (i.e., it is not governed by some other government organization) and governance over an entity generally recognized as a country.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: =1^isGovernedBy.gist:CountryGeoRegion; \u22640isGovernedBy.gist:GovernmentOrganization",
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:GovernmentOrganization & \u2203^isGovernedBy.gist:CountryGeoRegion)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "While a country government may enter into treaties with other country governments, there are no governing relationships among the treaty members."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Country Government"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:CountryGovernment"
      ],
      "is_a": "GovernmentOrganization",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/CountryGovernment",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "SubCountryGovernment"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "DegreeOfCommitment",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/DegreeOfCommitment",
      "description": "The difficulty of reversing a commitment.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A car rental typically has a lower degree of commitment than an airfare reservation.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Degree Of Commitment"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:DegreeOfCommitment"
      ],
      "is_a": "Category",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/DegreeOfCommitment",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Determination",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Determination",
      "description": "An event whose purpose is to establish a specific result, value, or outcome, usually by research, measuring, evaluating, or calculating.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Measuring the sulfur content of crude oil; evaluating a loan application for approval; estimating the price of gas for the next three months; determining whether and by how much an interest rate should change; classifying a purchase into a budget category.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Determination"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Determination"
      ],
      "close_mappings": [
        "iso22989:Decision"
      ],
      "is_a": "Event",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Determination",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Discipline",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Discipline",
      "description": "An area of study or practice.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Finance, accounting, project management, acoustics, ballistics.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Discipline"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Discipline"
