      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/GeoLocation",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "GeoPoint",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GeoPoint",
      "description": "An individual point on or above the Earth's surface, identified by latitude, longitude and altitude. Altitude is the distance measured from sea level. If altitude is missing, the point is assumed to be at the Earth's surface. These points are described using decimal latitude/longitude.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (\u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_altitude & \u2203latitude.xsd:double & \u2203longitude.xsd:double)"
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Geographic Point"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:GeoPoint"
      ],
      "is_a": "GeoLocation",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/GeoPoint",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "IntellectualProperty",
        "Intention",
        "Language",
        "Magnitude",
        "Organization",
        "PhysicalIdentifiableItem",
        "PhysicalSubstance",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "GeoRegion",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GeoRegion",
      "description": "A bounded region (or set of regions) on the surface of the Earth.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: (gist:GeoLocation & \u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_area)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "A geographic region could be non-contiguous; e.g., the region governed by the US federal government is the contiguous area of the lower 48 states plus Alaska, Hawaii, and overseas territories. Child classes in lower ontologies can make this distinction."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The bounded shape that defines the region occupied by Crater Lake; the bounded area known as the contiguous USA.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Geographic Region"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:GeoRegion"
      ],
      "is_a": "GeoLocation",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/GeoRegion",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "IntellectualProperty",
        "Intention",
        "Language",
        "Magnitude",
        "Organization",
        "PhysicalIdentifiableItem",
        "PhysicalSubstance",
        "Template",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "GeoRoute",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GeoRoute",
      "description": "An ordered set of geographic points that defines a path from a starting point to an ending point.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:OrderedCollection & \u2203^isMemberOf.gist:GeoPoint)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "A geographic route could describe a bus route by identifying the points where the bus stops. A geographic route could describe the boundary of a polygonal geographic region (it does not have to be a traveled route)."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Geographic Route"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:GeoRoute"
      ],
      "is_a": "OrderedCollection",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/GeoRoute",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "GeoVolume",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GeoVolume",
      "description": "A three-dimensional space on or near the surface of the Earth.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:GeoLocation & \u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_volume & \u2203^isGeoContainedIn.gist:GeoPoint)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "An oil reservoir, the body of a lake, or an airspace.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Geographic Volume"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:GeoVolume"
      ],
      "is_a": "GeoLocation",
