    {
      "name": "LivingThing",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/LivingThing",
      "description": "Something that is currently, or at some point in time was, alive.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:PhysicalIdentifiableItem & \u2203hasBiologicalParent.gist:LivingThing & =1birthDate)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Not all life forms have exactly two parents, so the restriction only specifies a minimum of one."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A cat, a mushroom, a tree.",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "Negative examples: fictional life forms such as unicorns or Mickey Mouse.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Living Thing"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:LivingThing"
      ],
      "is_a": "PhysicalIdentifiableItem",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/LivingThing",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Magnitude",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Magnitude",
      "description": "The amount of a measurable characteristic (aspect).",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (\u2203hasAspect.gist:Aspect & \u2203hasUnitOfMeasure.gist:UnitOfMeasure & \u2203numericValue.rdfs:Literal)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "An accuracy can be assigned to a magnitude using the property has accuracy."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A model of car could have a wheelbase of 113.2 inches. In this example, the aspect is wheelbase, the unit of measure is inch, and the numeric value is 113.2.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "see_also": [
        "gist:hasAccuracy"
      ],
      "aliases": [
        "Magnitude"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Magnitude"
      ],
      "close_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Quantity",
        "common_domain_model:Measure"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Price"
      ],
      "narrow_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Money"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Magnitude",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "Organization",
        "PhysicalIdentifiableItem",
        "PhysicalSubstance",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "MediaType",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/MediaType",
      "description": "A digitized type that computer applications can recognize.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: \u2203uniqueText.xsd:string"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "The unique text for an IANA media type is the concatenation of the 'Type name', a slash '/', and the 'Subtype name' as provided on the page displayed when you resolve the URI of the media type."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "application/sparql-results+xml",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "see_also": [
        "https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml"
      ],
      "aliases": [
        "Media Type"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:MediaType"
      ],
      "is_a": "Category",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/MediaType",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Medium",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Medium",
      "description": "A physical material on which a work can be rendered, represented, or implemented.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Paper, clay, a computer monitor.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Medium"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Medium"
      ],
      "is_a": "Category",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Medium",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Message",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Message",
      "description": "A specific instance of content sent from a sender to at least one other recipient.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:ContentExpression & \u2203comesFromAgent.(gist:Organization | gist:Person) & \u2203goesToAgent.(gist:Organization | gist:Person))"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "An email, voice, or web service message; a phone call.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Message"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Message"
      ],
      "is_a": "ContentExpression",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Message",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Network",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Network",
      "description": "A composite consisting of nodes connected by links.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Composite & \u2203^isMemberOf.(gist:NetworkLink | gist:NetworkNode))"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A physical network could include connected computers or routers, whereas a social network would consist of related person or organization members (or their proxies, such as accounts).",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Network"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Network"
      ],
      "is_a": "Composite",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Network",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "NetworkLink",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/NetworkLink",
      "description": "An abstract representation of the connection between two or more nodes in a network.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: \u2200links.gist:NetworkNode; =2links",
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Component & \u2203isMemberOf.gist:Network & \u2203links.gist:NetworkNode)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Each network link is connected to a network node via the property gist:links or one of its subproperties."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A network link may be physical, such as pipes, wired or wireless networks, but may also be a link in a non-physical network, such as organizational structures or social networks.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Network Link"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:NetworkLink"
      ],
      "is_a": "Component",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/NetworkLink",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "NetworkNode",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/NetworkNode",
      "description": "A node in a network.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: \u2203isMemberOf.gist:Network"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A person's account is a node in a social network; a valve is a node in a network of pipes.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Network Node"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:NetworkNode"
      ],
      "is_a": "Component",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/NetworkNode",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Offer",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Offer",
      "description": "A contingent commitment to buy, sell, swap or provide one or more described or identified goods or services in exchange for another (or others).",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:ContingentObligation & \u2203hasGiver.(gist:Organization | gist:Person) & \u2203offersToProvide.owl:Thing & \u2203offersToReceive.owl:Thing & \u2203plannedEndDateTime.xsd:dateTime & \u2203plannedStartDateTime.xsd:dateTime)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Dates on an offer represent the time period the offer is valid for, as in '25% off through October 25, 2025.'"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "An offer to sell a book for a given price; an offer to purchase real estate for a particular price; an offer to swap a sea kayak for a mountain bike; currency exchange. A donation may be modeled as an offer to receive money typically in exchange for $0.00, but sometimes for items of value such as coffee mugs or T-shirts.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Offer"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Offer"
      ],
      "is_a": "ContingentObligation",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Offer",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "OrderedCollection",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/OrderedCollection",
      "description": "A collection whose members are ordered in some way.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Collection & (\u2203^isFirstMemberOf.gist:OrderedMember | =0^isMemberOf) & \u2200^isMemberOf.gist:OrderedMember)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Includes partially ordered collections as well as collections in which members occupy the same position in a 'tie.' All members of an ordered collection are ordered members."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Ordered Collection"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:OrderedCollection"
      ],
      "is_a": "Collection",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/OrderedCollection",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "OrderedMember",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/OrderedMember",
      "description": "A member of an ordered collection serving as a proxy for a real world item, which can appear in different orders in different collections. The ordered member appears in exactly one ordered collection.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Component & (\u2203precedesDirectly.gist:OrderedMember | \u2203^precedesDirectly.gist:OrderedMember | \u2203sequence.xsd:integer) & \u2203providesOrderFor.owl:Thing & \u2200isMemberOf.gist:OrderedCollection & =1isMemberOf)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "An ordered member points to the real world item via the providesOrderFor property. Ordering information is represented either as a number in a sequence, or by preceding or following another ordered member."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A person may rank 12th in the Boston Marathon but 29th in the New York City Marathon.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Ordered Member"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:OrderedMember"
      ],
      "is_a": "Component",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/OrderedMember",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Organization",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Organization",
      "description": "A structured entity formed to achieve specific goals, typically involving members with defined roles.",
      "comments": [
        "Not all organizations have members, e.g. shell companies.",
        "While typically the members of organizations are people, in some cases they are other organizations; e.g., the members of the United Nations are country governments."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Legal entities like companies; non-legal entities like clubs, committees, or departments.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Organization"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Organization"
      ],
      "close_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:LegalEntity"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "dpv:ThirdParty"
      ],
      "narrow_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:BusinessUnit",
        "dpv:OrganisationalUnit",
        "iso22989:Organization"
      ],
      "broad_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Party",
        "dpv:LegalEntity"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Organization",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "PhysicalIdentifiableItem",
        "PhysicalSubstance",
        "SchemaMetaData",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Permission",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Permission",
      "description": "A description of things one is permitted to do.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Intention & \u2203allows.gist:Behavior)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Permission could be broad, such as free speech, but more often is very specific, such as the right to enter a particular property.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Permission"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Permission"
      ],
      "exact_mappings": [
        "dpv:Permission"
      ],
      "is_a": "Intention",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Permission",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Person",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Person",
      "description": "A human being who was or is alive.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: \u2200hasBiologicalParent.gist:Person",
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:LivingThing & \u2203hasBiologicalParent.gist:Person)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Negative example: fictional characters.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Person"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Person"
      ],
      "exact_mappings": [
        "dpv:NaturalPerson"
      ],
      "close_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:NaturalPerson"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "iso22989:AIUser",
        "iso22989:DataSubject"
      ],
      "narrow_mappings": [
        "dpv:DataSubject"
      ],
      "broad_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Party"
      ],
      "is_a": "LivingThing",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Person",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "PhysicalActionType",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/PhysicalActionType",
      "description": "A category indicating the type of an action based on its effect in the physical world.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Lifting a garage door, turning off a valve, dropping cadmium rods.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Physical Action Type"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:PhysicalActionType"
      ],
      "is_a": "Category",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/PhysicalActionType",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "PhysicalAddress",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/PhysicalAddress",
      "description": "An address that refers to a locatable place within the physical universe.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Address & \u2203refersTo.gist:GeoLocation)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "1600 Pennsylvania Avenue NW, Washington, DC 20500; PO Box 7704, San Francisco, CA 94120-7704; Room 317 in the Louvre Museum.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Physical Address"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:PhysicalAddress"
      ],
      "close_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Address"
      ],
      "is_a": "Address",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/PhysicalAddress",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "PhysicalAddressType",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/PhysicalAddressType",
      "description": "A category indicating local customary characterizations of physical addresses.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Street address, PO box, FPO code.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Physical Address Type"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:PhysicalAddressType"
      ],
      "is_a": "Category",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/PhysicalAddressType",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "PhysicalEvent",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/PhysicalEvent",
      "description": "An event that can be said to have occurred at some place in space.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Event & \u2203occursIn.gist:GeoLocation)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A meeting, a car accident.",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "Negative examples: Excludes events that have no meaningful location, such as financial events or project milestones.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Physical Event"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:PhysicalEvent"
      ],
      "is_a": "Event",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/PhysicalEvent",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "PhysicalIdentifiableItem",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/PhysicalIdentifiableItem",
      "description": "A discrete physical object which, if subdivided, will result in parts that are distinguishable in nature from the whole and in general also from the other parts.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: \u2203isMadeUpOf.gist:PhysicalSubstance; \u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_mass; \u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_volume"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "This concept generally corresponds to count nouns in English. By contrast, physical substances, such as an amount of water, flour, or sand, are mass nouns. Physical identifiable items are made up of physical substances; e.g., a cake is made up of butter, flour, and sugar; a statue is made of bronze. If you divide a physical substance such as an amount of water into parts, you have two amounts of water otherwise indistinguishable from one another; if you divide a physical identifiable item such as a computer into parts, each part is different from the whole."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A laptop, a physical book, a car, a building, a landmark (such as a tree stump with an etched marking to denote a campsite).",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Physical Identifiable Item"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:PhysicalIdentifiableItem"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/PhysicalIdentifiableItem",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "SchemaMetaData",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "PhysicalSubstance",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/PhysicalSubstance",
      "description": "An undifferentiated amount of physical material which, when subdivided, results in each part being indistinguishable in nature from the whole and from every other part.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: \u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_volume; \u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_mass"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "An instance of this class has weight and takes up space. We mean the physical gold in a ring, not the concept of gold that shows up in the periodic table. The latter would be an instance of gist:KnowledgeConcept.",
        "This concept generally corresponds to mass nouns in English. By contrast, instances of gist:PhysicalIdentifiableItem, such as a computer, book, or car, are count nouns. Physical identifiable items are made up of physical substances; e.g., a cake is made up of butter, flour, and sugar; a ring is made of gold. If you divide a physical substance such as an amount of water into parts, you have different amounts of water otherwise indistinguishable from one another; if you divide a physical identifiable item such as a computer into parts, each part will be distinguishable from the original whole."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "An amount of water, penicillin, sand, or gold.",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "Negative example: the concept of gold.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Physical Substance"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:PhysicalSubstance"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/PhysicalSubstance",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
