      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Specification",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Specification",
      "description": "The set of characteristics and constraints on their values that specify what it means to be a particular type of thing, such as a material, product, service or event. A specification is sufficiently precise to allow evaluating conformance to the specification.",
      "comments": [
        "Although a characterization of how to do something is often called a specification, the intended meaning here is limited to specifying what something is. The focus is on the what, not the how. Use gist:TaskTemplate for specifying the how, such as a plan or process specification. Use gist:conformsTo to assert that something conforms to a specification. To represent a definition of a particular type of thing that is not sufficiently precise to be a gist:Specification, consider using gist:KnowledgeConcept."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The specification of the iPhone 14; hypothetical events covered by a homeowner's insurance policy; a drug quality specification - a set of acceptance criteria for quality characteristics that must be controlled to ensure a drug is fit for its intended use.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Specification"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Specification"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:EligibleCollateralCriteria"
      ],
      "is_a": "Intention",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Specification",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "SubCountryGovernment",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/SubCountryGovernment",
      "description": "The government of a governed geographic region other than a country which is under the direct or indirect control of a country government.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:GovernmentOrganization & \u2203isGovernedBy.gist:CountryGovernment & \u2203^isGovernedBy.gist:GeoRegion)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Note that the predicate gist:isGovernedBy is used both for the relationship a governed geographic region has to its government and for the relationship a sub-region government has to the government of the larger region.",
        "There are many types of sub-regions of a country and the governments thereof (as well as different terms, like 'province' and 'state,' which refer to essentially the same type of thing). We should not automatically assume 'state,' 'county,' and 'city.' Subclasses or categories can be defined if greater specificity is needed.",
        "This class applies only to organizations governing geographic regions. Regulatory and bureaucratic organizations are members of the more generic gist:GovernmentOrganization class."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Sub-Country Government"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:SubCountryGovernment"
      ],
      "is_a": "GovernmentOrganization",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/SubCountryGovernment",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "System",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/System",
      "description": "A composite made up of interacting or interdependent components that together operate as a whole.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Composite & \u2203^isDirectPartOf.gist:Component)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "May be used to refer to either man-made or natural systems."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A manufacturing system, a storm system.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "System"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:System"
      ],
      "is_a": "Composite",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/System",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tag",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Tag",
      "description": "A term in a folksonomy used to categorize things. Tags can be made up on the fly by users.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: \u2203containedText.xsd:string"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Whether to use gist:containedText or gist:uniqueText on tags is an implementation decision. Since the latter is a subproperty of the former, the restriction remains valid either way."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Tag"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Tag"
      ],
      "is_a": "Category",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Tag",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Task",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Task",
      "description": "An activity or piece of work that is either proposed, planned, scheduled, underway, or completed.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Event & \u2203hasGoal.gist:Intention)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Something that could potentially be executed, which is merely described but not proposed in any specific way, such as a business process for onboarding a new employee, or the steps in a recipe for making polyethylene from ethylene, is not a task but rather a task template.",
        "This term is broader than the English word 'task,' which implies assignment, responsibility, or duty. In ordinary English going to a concert has a goal but is (generally) done for pleasure rather than out of obligation, and would not be considered a task, while according to the gist definition it is a task. The expansion of meaning is deliberate, so that anything that has a goal and can be specified by a task template is a task.",
        "Use the property gist:isBasedOn to link a task back to the task template."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Task"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Task"
      ],
      "related_mappings": [
        "common_domain_model:Workflow",
        "iso22989:Task"
      ],
      "is_a": "Event",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Task",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "TaskTemplate",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/TaskTemplate",
      "description": "An outline of a task of a particular type, which is the basis for executing such tasks.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:Template & \u2203hasGoal.gist:Intention)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "A task template may define a single activity or a series of activities; the level of granularity can be varied according to use case. For example, in a new employee onboarding process, signing up for benefits might be one activity, or it might be broken down into signing up for health insurance, signing up for dental insurance, etc.",
        "Use the property isBasedOn to link the Task back to the TaskTemplate."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A business process for onboarding new employees.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Task Template"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:TaskTemplate"
      ],
      "is_a": "Template",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/TaskTemplate",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Template",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Template",
      "description": "Something used to make objects in its own image.",
      "comments": [
        "Use gist:isBasedOn to link the object made from the template back to the template."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A die in manufacturing is used to make stamped parts; a form provides a structure and fields to be filled in; a cookie cutter is a template for cookies.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Template"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Template"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Template",
      "disjoint_with": [
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "TemporalRelation",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/TemporalRelation",
      "description": "A relationship existing for a period of time.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: =1startDateTime; \u22652hasParticipant"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "A temporal relation must have a minimum of two participants. For example, both the employer and the employee are participants in a temporal relation representing a period of employment. Note that 'participant' does not imply agency; a non-sentient being can participate in a temporal relation. For example, both a person and a house could be participants in a hypothetical relation 'lives at.'"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The relationship between a person and their employer; the relationship between a person or business and an address.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Temporal Relation"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:TemporalRelation"
      ],
      "mixins": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/TemporalRelation",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Text",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/Text",
      "description": "Content expressed as a written sequence of characters.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:ContentExpression & \u2203isExpressedIn.gist:Language & \u2203containedText.xsd:string)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Text is expressed in a language (human or computer) and may but need not specify an encoding."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Negative example: photographs or scans of text are not text. These instead depict a subject, which happens to be text.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "aliases": [
        "Text"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "gist:Text"
      ],
      "is_a": "ContentExpression",
      "slots": [
        "name",
        "description"
      ],
      "slot_usage": {},
      "class_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/Text",
      "@type": "ClassDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "TimeInterval",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/TimeInterval",
      "description": "A span of time with a known start time, end time, and duration. As long as two of the three are known, the third can be inferred.",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: =1startDateTime; =1hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_duration; =1endDateTime"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "An ongoing state of affairs with an unknown end time in the future cannot be a time interval; e.g. the lifespan of a living person cannot be a time interval, as the end time is unknown.",
        "This is distinct from a duration, which describes how long a time interval lasts (e.g., one hour; 3 days; 22 minutes)."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "7pm to 9pm on Jan 1, 2001; fiscal year 2023 (according to some particular definition of fiscal year); the week starting at midnight of January 12, 2023 and lasting exactly 168 hours.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
